-- title:
--   Representability of mathcal O_D-stable subgroup ideals by a projective scheme
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $B_0$ be a commutative ring, and let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B_0$ in the sense of the structure `FormalODModule`: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $B_0$, an action $a \mapsto \Phi.\mathrm{act}\,a$ of $\mathbb Z_{p^2} =$ `Zp2 p` (the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{p^2}$) by pairs of power series which are endomorphisms of $F$, and a further endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\sigma a]\circ\varpi$. Let $N, h \in \mathbb N$, and assume the kernel algebra $B_0[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/\big(\mathrm{act}\,(p^N)\big)$ is a finite free $B_0$-module and that the images of $x_0, x_1$ in it are nilpotent. Then there are a scheme $H$, a morphism $q : H \to \operatorname{Spec} B_0$, and, for every $B_0$-algebra $S$, a bijection $\mathrm{pt}\,S$ between the set of ideals $I \subseteq S[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ such that (1) $S[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/I$ is a finite $S$-module, (2) it is projective, (3) for every field $\kappa$ and ring homomorphism $f : S \to \kappa$ the $\kappa$-dimension of $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/f(I)$ is $p^h$, (4) $x_i^e \in I$ for both $i$ and some $e$, (5) every element of $I$ has zero constant coefficient, (6) for $f \in I$ the series $f(F_S(x,y))$ lies in the ideal generated by the images of $I$ under $x \mapsto x^{\mathrm{inl}}$ and $x \mapsto x^{\mathrm{inr}}$, (7) $I$ is stable under substitution of $\mathrm{act}\,a$ for every $a \in \mathbb Z_{p^2}$, (8) $I$ is stable under substitution of $\varpi$, and (9) both components of $\mathrm{act}\,(p^N)$ lie in $I$ — all for $\Phi_S =$ `Φ.map (algebraMap B₀ S)` — and the set of morphisms $g : \operatorname{Spec} S \to H$ with $g$ followed by $q$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $B_0 \to S$; moreover these nine conditions are preserved by base change $I \mapsto I\,S'[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ along any $B_0$-algebra map $\varphi : S \to S'$, the bijections are natural, i.e. $\mathrm{pt}\,S'$ applied to the base-changed ideal equals $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $\mathrm{pt}\,S\,(I)$, and there are $m \in \mathbb N$ and a closed immersion $\iota_P$ from $H$ into $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded ring of homogeneous polynomials in $m+1$ variables over $B_0$ with $\iota_P$ followed by `ProjSpace.π B₀ m` equal to $q$.
--
--   This is the representability half of the construction of the Hilbert-type moduli scheme of finite locally free $\mathcal O_D$-stable subgroup schemes of degree $p^h$ inside $\Phi[p^N]$, in the form used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the functor of such subgroup ideals is represented by a $B_0$-scheme that is projective over $\operatorname{Spec} B_0$, the closed immersion into projective space over $B_0$ being part of the assertion. It feeds the assembly of the moduli package for special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.ModuliPackage.exists_scheme_nilpPoints_equiv_subtype_act_pow_mem_span_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.ModuliPackage.exists_scheme_nilpPoints_equiv_subtype_act_pow_mem_span_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace).
